<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Just updated to the aplpha 2.2 version and I cannot decrease the power.<br><br>Holding pressed P2 button increases the power to max, but there is no way to decrease it.<br><br>Manual says "SK2+Left" decreases and "SK2+Right" increases power. Which is Right and which is Left ?<br><br>Also, holding pressed the P1 button does nothing.</div></blockquote>Read the initial post. <br><br>P1 = Left<br>P2 = Right<br><br>Don't hold down P1 or P2 when changing power. The functionality is designed to prevent accidental change in power caused by buttons being held in.<br>Holding P2 when on 5W has special functionality<br><br>See the USER GUIDE</div></blockquote>But if you keep "P2" pressed <span style="text-decoration:underline">at any power level</span> it will go up to "+W+" (which is user defined power level).<br><br>This makes it confusing, since it should mean that keeping "P1" pressed should have the reverse effect.<br><br>Could not find an updated guide for MD2017, all I could find were the already supported models, where it says "SK1" and "SK2" which I tough that they were "P1" and "P2" respectively as it mapps easy in my brain.</div></blockquote>The SK2+longpress P2 (or Right key on other platforms) is a safety measure, as the operator really insist to use higest DAC level for the PA drive.<br>Lowering power on the other hand don't need such safety thing, it works the same for all power levels.<br><br>About the user guide, the MD-2017 has only one reference at the moment. The firmware is in Alpha stage, and things could still change a lot, we can't waste time to write and rewrite multiple times various parts of the manual.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Thu Mar 07, 2024 7:39 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
